# Dependencies and build output — never committed; reproducible via package-lock.json
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# Environment files are the single most dangerous file in this repo.
# This app processes children's voice data and vendor API keys; a leaked .env
# is a privacy incident. Only .env.example (which holds no secrets) is committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Runtime data: audio clips, generated illustrations, SQLite scratch files.
# Audio retention is enforced server-side; nothing should ever live in git.
#
# Both roots are listed because the server resolves its cache dirs from the
# CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY: `docker compose` runs from the repo root (/data),
# while `npm run dev -w @qissa/server` runs from the workspace
# (packages/server/data). Only the first was ignored, so a local dev run left
# real child audio clips sitting untracked in a PUBLIC repository, one
# `git add -A` away from being published.
#
# Anchored, not bare: `data/` would also swallow packages/core/src/data, which
# is the phonics curriculum and must stay committed.
/data/
/packages/server/data/
data-runtime/
*.log

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local diagnostic scratch from manual vendor tests - never part of the product.
diag-clip.wav
flux-test.png
illustration-styled.png

# Scratch images from manual vendor probes (character-reference checks etc).
ref-probe-*.png

# `npm run review` output — a frank external critique of our own product,
# written to the repo root for convenience. This repository is PUBLIC; a
# ranked list of our weaknesses is not something to publish by accident.
review-output.md

# Prisma — generated client is derived from schema.prisma, never committed
packages/server/prisma/generated/
